synthesis.parity_verdict:
Structurally, ServicioSAP's credit method is close to LAN; in business terms it is not yet equivalent. What matches LAN:
- the order of operations: group by SKU, build the 'cantidad,sku' list plus SEGU00001, SMS lookup, validated-phone lookup, existence-only gate, header insert, per-line insert, promo burn after the lines;
- the gate rule itself: existence only in both, with no balance check in either (LAN's checkSaldo always returns 0, so runbook §16 is confirmed);
- the 59-column header INSERT with SCOPE_IDENTITY;
- a faithful three-valued port of the ValidacionTelefono IF (SP_CREDITO_WEB_DATOS.sql:210-221 against SolicitudCreditoWebMethods.cs:312-328);
- line pricing with the DescuentoCategoria CEILING, Orden numbering and the duplicate-SKU skip;
- the partial-failure outcome: a failed line leaves the header plus earlier lines, no promo burn, and a success answer.

What keeps it from matching LAN today:
- One hard blocker (D1/Q1): with no parameter Size, every real payload's metodoEnvio 'tablerate_bestway', and 'NO ESPECIFICADO' for any BP whose Gender is not 1/2, raise SQL error 8152. So once Magento sends BPs, not one real credit application can be written.
- Divergences that change stored data:
  - the validated-phone input: two ServicioSAP copies of LAN's single rule, and both differ from it (Q4);
  - an orphan header when the condition cannot be resolved (Q5);
  - an unverified SIGMAVI condition mapping (Q6);
  - promoter coupons: different table, a gate at burn time, all free rows stamped, and a promoter's first sale no longer attributed (Q7/Q8);
  - placeholder phones where LAN wrote nothing (Q10);
  - master-data fields: birth date NULL, estadoCivil '', Namemiddle dropped, sexo mapping (Q11, Q14, Q19, Q1);
  - cost fixed at 0, no TELEFONIA region SKU, origen fixed (Q15, Q17, Q18);
  - an unescaped SKU in the SD29 filter, which may silently drop '+' SKUs.

Liberador and callback are still commented out (R3), and Magento ignores the setOrder body (CreditoOrderManagement.php:53-76). So no credit order completes end to end whether ServicioSAP succeeds or fails; errors are visible only in sap.log.

